m>Clematis</em> 'Kakio' (EL)","entityDescription":"A climber 2.5-3m high with green leaves and flowers, 12-16cm across, composed of six to ten, usually eight, purplish pink sepals with paler pink centres, and yellow stamens, in early summer and again in late summer and early autumn; many clematis are visited by bees for pollen, and some also provide nectar","image":"RHS_RHS-0004440_11663.JPG","commonName":"clematis 'Kakio'","nurseriesCount":6,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":45411,"botanicalName":"<em>Clematis</em> 'Kiri Te Kanawa' (EL)","entityDescription":"A deciduous climber to about 2.5m, with mid-green foliage, flowering in late spring to early summer on last year’s growth, and in early autumn on new growth. The double flowers are 10-15cm across with broad petals and cream stamens; early flowers are deep, rich purple, late ones are paler","image":"moja01547.jpg","commonName":"clematis 'Kiri Te Kanawa'","nurseriesCount":3,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":379003,"botanicalName":"<em>Clematis</em> 'Kokonoe'<sup>PBR</sup> (LL/d)","entityDescription":"A deciduous climber to 2.5m tall with dark green foliage and deep purple flowers borne from late spring into autumn. The first flowers borne in early spring emerge as singles but later blooms are doubles with an inner ruff-like ring of tepals","image":"Press-Chelsea2019_2Z5A9222_14360.jpg","commonName":"clematis 'Kokonoe'","nurseriesCount":11,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":{"plantId":379003,"price":"£29.99","oldPrice":null,"url":"https://www.rhsplants.co.uk/plants/_/clematis-kokonoe-pbr/classid.2000033509/sku.PL30004233/"}},{"id":89349,"botanicalName":"<em>Clematis</em> 'Lady Northcliffe' (EL)","entityDescription":"'Lady Northcliffe' is a climber 1.5-3m high with green leaves and flowers 10-15cm across, composed of usually six overlapping, wide, broadly elliptic, wavy-edged sepals, rich violet-blue at first then fading to mid lavender-blue, and creamy stamens, from midsummer to early autumn and sometimes later; many clematis are visited by bees for pollen, and some also provide nectar","image":"RHS_WSYD0003572_11664.JPG","commonName":"clematis 'Lady Northcliffe'","nurseriesCount":3,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":99627,"botanicalName":"<em>Clematis</em> 'Lasurstern' (EL)","entityDescription":"A medium-sized vigorous deciduous climber. Flowers produced from old wood are 18-22cm in width, with 7-8 overlapping deep lavender-blue, wavy-edged sepals and prominent cream stamens.  Flowers late spring to early summer and late summer followed by large spherical seedheads.","image":"WSY0035573_3860.jpg","commonName":"clematis 'Lasurstern'","nurseriesCount":12,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":328373,"botanicalName":"<em>Clematis</em> 'Lemon Beauty' (A)","entityDescription":"A deciduous climber, to around 3m high, with toothed, mid-green leaves borne in groups of three. Nodding, bell-shaped, lightly scented pale lemon yellow flowers are produced in late spring on the previous year's growth. New growth often produces further flowers in mid to late summer","image":"","commonName":"clematis 'Lemon Beauty'","nurseriesCount":3,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":57365,"botanicalName":"<em>Clematis</em> 'Lilactime' (EL)","entityDescription":"A compact climber producing large, semi-double, light violet-blue flowers 15-20cm wide with white filaments and magenta anthers from late spring to early summer, with some single flowers appearing in early autumn","image":"WSY0004486_4606.jpg","commonName":"clematis 'Lilactime'","nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":269518,"botanicalName":"<em>Clematis</em> 'Little Mermaid' (EL)","entityDescription":"A deciduous climber to about 2.5m, with light green foliage, flowering from early to mid-summer on last year’s growth, and in late summer to early autumn on new growth. Flowers may be single or semi-double, 8-12cm across, and are salmon-pink, sometimes showing a purple central stripe, with creamy-yellow stamens","image":"blwa01103.jpg","commonName":"clematis 'Little Mermaid'","nurseriesCount":3,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":382777,"botanicalName":"<em>Clematis</em> 'Long Tall Sally' (V)","entityDescription":"'Long Tall Sally' is a climber to 2m tall with nodding, tubular flowers to 4cm long comprising 4 tepals fused along their length with tips free and curving outwards Flowers are lilac-purple at the base and creamy-white at the tips and are followed by persistent seedheads","image":"ClemLONG_TALL_SALLY__BBB_1.jpg","commonName":"clematis 'Long Tall Sally'","nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":80498,"botanicalName":"<em>Clematis</em> 'Louise Rowe' (EL)","entityDescription":"A deciduous climber, flowering in early summer on old wood, and again in late summer to early autumn on new wood. Flowers are 10-15cm across, pale greyish mauve, with a green flush in the centre of the petals, fully double, with twisted central petals at the start of the season, then semi-double then single","image":"RHS_PUB0010330_11729.JPG","commonName":"clematis 'Louise Rowe'","nurseriesCount":2,"synonymPar